AWS CodePipeline

What is AWS CodePipeline?

AWS CodePipeline is a fully managed continuous delivery service that automates the stages required to release software.

It orchestrates different CI/CD services.

Typical Pipeline

Source
  ↓
Build
  ↓
Test
  ↓
Deploy

Example AWS pipeline:

CodeCommit
    ↓
CodeBuild
    ↓
CodeDeploy
    ↓
EC2

Main Components

Source Stage

Gets the latest source code.

Examples:

- AWS CodeCommit
- GitHub
- Amazon S3

Build Stage

Builds and tests the application.

Example:

- AWS CodeBuild

Deploy Stage

Deploys the application.

Examples:

- AWS CodeDeploy
- Amazon ECS
- AWS Elastic Beanstalk

Approval Stage

Can require manual approval before production deployment.

Build
 ↓
Test
 ↓
Manual Approval
 ↓
Production

CodePipeline Execution

When a new change is detected:

Developer Push
      ↓
Source Stage
      ↓
Build Stage
      ↓
Test
      ↓
Approval
      ↓
Deploy
      ↓
Production

CodePipeline Benefits

- Automates software release process
- Connects different AWS services
- Supports third-party tools
- Provides continuous delivery
- Reduces manual deployment steps
- Improves release consistency

